# Evidence corpora are byte-exact records: SHA256SUMS files, bundle manifests
# and recorded hashes bind every file. `-text` turns off end-of-line conversion
# (core.autocrlf, core.eol), so every clone reproduces the committed bytes,
# CRLFs and terminal CRs included; git still shows text diffs for text content.
# `-whitespace` keeps `git diff --check` and `git apply --whitespace=fix` from
# flagging or rewriting the trailing spaces, CRs and blank lines that evidence
# must keep. Attributes do not rewrite committed blobs; they apply to checkouts
# and to evidence added from now on.
docs/benchmarks/** -text -whitespace
docs/specs/*/evidence/** -text -whitespace
# Authored scripts and narrative beside the corpora keep the configured
# whitespace checks (`!whitespace` restores the core.whitespace default).
docs/benchmarks/*.md !whitespace
docs/benchmarks/jail/*.md !whitespace
docs/benchmarks/jail/*.py !whitespace
